Sat Nov 21 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Add tkdesk-num-lbs.patch: file browsers opened with the default 3
  listboxes, ignoring both the number saved in _layout and
  tkdesk(num_lbs) from the System config (Itcl 3+ applies the
  constructor options only after the listboxes are built)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Fri Nov 13 03:00:00 UTC 2026 - caiocco <caiocco@yahoo.com.br>

- Initial package of TkDesk 2.0
  * Upstream patches 2.0p1 and 2.0p2 plus the Debian 2.0-14 patch
    set (Itcl 4 / Tcl 8.6 port, safe temporary files, GCC 15); the
    dpkg-specific menu changes in Debian's configs are left out
  * Use TkDesk's bundled BLT subset instead of a system BLT, ported
    to Tk 8.6 on 64-bit (tkdesk-blt-tk86.patch): real tkInt.h
    instead of copied Tk 8.0-8.4 structures, all allocations through
    Tcl's allocator (fixes "free(): invalid size" at start-up),
    pointer-sized channel handles and Tcl_Pids (fixes empty Disk
    Usage window), any Tk 8.6.x accepted
  * Load [incr Tcl] 4 from the tcl package via package require
  * tkdesk-server-key.patch: enabling the TkDesk server no longer
    aborts on the missing /dev/kmem; its access key comes from
    /dev/urandom instead of a pid-seeded generator, and it only
    listens on 127.0.0.1
  * tkdesk-xdg-open.patch: open URLs with xdg-open
  * Build with optflags (drop the Makefile's -O), no empty RUNPATH
  * Add a desktop entry and icon
